The guard captain has a 50% chance of carrying a silver saber, and 50%
chance of a long sword. Greyswandir can be wished for, or can be
sacrificed for.

The Vorpal Blade has a +5 to hit and a +1 to damage (the spoilers call
this a "+d1"...). That's not its prime ability, though. It's best
ability is its ability to behead. With every hit, you have 5% chance to
instantly kill a monster. This comes in handy with monsters that
teleport away to head, then come back at full HP. From the spoilers
(art1-343.txt):

Vorpal Blade
